{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1130157-lesser-ministries-anyone","id":1130157,"title":"Lesser Ministries anyone?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-08-16T23:19:26-07:00","id":1130157,"title":"Lesser Ministries anyone?","content":"Hi Wise Willworkers, Dusk here. <br /> <br /> Due to some friends of mine possibly getting into Mage the Awakening recently I delved back into some of my old PDFs, and as always had to re-read my favorite Mage Supplement: the Seers of the Throne Order book. I absolutely love those despicable bastards, and I might have gotten a bit carried away and made a few Lesser Ministries for possible future Mage Chronicles (technically I made two and updated one I made a while ago.) I feel compelled to share them with those who're interested in that sort of thing, and ask that if anyone else wants to share their own ideas or write ups for Lesser Ministries then if there isn't already a thread for that then there will be now. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> I short handed these to save word count, so they may be simplistic write ups. But I hope if nothing else they help illustrate why these shameless sellouts are so fascinating to me, and why they make such great foils for the Pentacle. <br /> <br /> <br /> \u2022 Homebrew Ministries <br /> <br /> ~ Penumbra<br /> &gt; Motto: &quot;Normality casts the darkest shadow.&quot;<br /> &gt; Patron Exarch: The Nemesis.<br /> &gt; Minister: Relleus, Seneschal of the Weeping Moon.<br /> &gt; Tyranny: Normalize society's ills and failings, demonize everything unacceptable in society.<br /> &gt; Allies: Hegemony, Paternoster, and secretly Mammon (hedging bets for Hegemony's fall.)<br /> &gt; Rivals: Praetorian, and Lesser Ministries dedicated to war and the dissolution of society.<br /> &gt; Plots: Investigation into the spirit-hybrid swarm entities, sometimes referred to as the Host by Shapechangers, has increased in recent years as the Ministry seeks to create Servitors of their very own. If such a creature could be domesticated then it would be an invaluable means of control due to it's naturally invasive nature. <br /> &gt; Failings: The direct manipulation of Spirits and the Gauntlet as a means of influencing the Shadow has drawn a lot of unwanted attention over the years. Suffice to say, the Ministry has it's fair share of enemies from both Spirits, Shapechangers, and sensitive Sleepwalkers alike. <br /> &gt; Mysteries: Exarchal messages in High Speech hidden in popular advertisements and brand logos. The lost names of ancient Gods of fear, alienation, and complacency. A silver blade engraved with words in the tongue of the Spirits that grants it's wielder Renowned amongst the Spirits so long as they prove worthy. <br /> &gt; Inspiration: Of course the Ministry's namesake, but also Pentex and other corporate evils that utilizes the spirit realm as a raw resource. <br /> <br /> <br /> ~ Hyades<br /> &gt; Motto: &quot;Abandon hope.&quot;<br /> &gt; Patron Exarch: The Ruin.<br /> &gt; Minister: Lorrian II, King of the Shrouded City.<br /> &gt; Tyranny: Cultivate defeatism and escapism through despair, tedium, and self-destructive habits. <br /> &gt; Allies: All four Great Ministries.<br /> &gt; Rivals: All other Lesser Ministries.<br /> &gt; Plots: The Ministry currently has Pylons working on weaponizing both corporate America and drug culture to further the Exarch's goals, but has yet to make inroads into the entertainment industry. Hyades seeks to remedy that as soon as possible since recent auguries indicate that doing so would allow further expansion for the Ministry.<br /> &gt; Failings: The Ministry is small compared to even some of the other Lesser Ministries. Hyades' reach only really extends to the Pacific North West of North America, and even then there are some regional Nameless Orders that are still larger in scope and influence. The fact that they remain active to this day is solely because they made themselves invaluable to the region's Tetrarchy.<br /> &gt; Mysteries: Artwork depicting abstract prophesies made by depressed Sleeper artists. A living office complex that feeds off the literal hopes and dreams of it's workers. A narcotic drug that traps non-lucid dreamers in an Astral Realm of languor while their bodies become comatose and highly susceptible to magical manipulation. <br /> &gt; Inspiration: Contemporary depictions of the King in Yellow's servants, and some depictions of the Lotus Eaters from the Odyssey. <br /> <br /> <br /> ~ Charon<br /> &gt; Motto: &quot;As in life, so in death.&quot;<br /> &gt; Patron Exarch: The Psychopomp.<br /> &gt; Minister: The Director (It's not what it seems.)<br /> &gt; Tyranny: Manipulate people's worldly passions in life so that their anchors will be more easily controllable after death.<br /> &gt; Allies: Panopticon, Praetorian, and Mammon. <br /> &gt; Rivals: Paternoster, and all Lesser Ministries truly loyal to the Psychopomp. (More on that soon.)<br /> &gt; Plots: Charon's greatest asset is it's corporate Mystery Cult, Fulcrum International. In recent years the Ministry has invested countless resources into making it's pet corporation into a true power player in the world market. Today it can rival companies like the Deva Corporation and Last Dynasty International, and hungrily consumes lesser players into it's growing list of subsidiaries. <br /> &gt; Failings: The problem with Charon is that it's a Heretical Ministry. It's Minister, if it ever truly had one, has long been replaced by a powerful supernatural entity known only as the Director. While the Director still fulfills the same role as Minister, it's agenda is clearly more geared towards controlling ghosts and growing it's Mystery Cult. (The true nature of the Director is left purposefully vague so that it can better fit the needs of one's individual Chronicle. The only thing known for certain about it is that whether or not it's Supernal in nature it's well aware of the Wise and took over their organization so it could utilize their Supernal powers. One of my favorite personal theory about the Director is thus: It's the Supernal Symbol of Fulcrum International itself. The Ministry's use of the company as a sympathetic symbol led to it gaining Supernal weight and awareness. It see's itself as a nascent Exarch and seeks to use the Ministry to perform a &quot;hostile takeover&quot; and devour the Exarch of Death, thus replacing them.)<br /> &gt; Mysteries: Factories in the Underworld that mirror abandoned Fulcrum Facilities and staffed by the ghosts of former employees. Unique ghosts and other chthonic entities that defy the laws death. Bleeding-edge technology that serves as an anchor for ghosts, creating mechanical-ghost Claimed. <br /> &gt; Inspiration: Obviously Pentex and the Umbrella Corporation, but also Praxis from the podcast Alice Isn't Dead.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3436,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage","user":"Dusksage","date":".  Spellcheck 08-17-2017, 02:21 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage","name":"Dusksage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3436_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-17T00:06:08-07:00","id":1130164,"title":"","content":"Maybe this falls under Mammon, but I feel like there should be a Ministry whose philosophy is built around the Huxlian model of tyranny - keeping the populace in a docile content haze. Mammon consumerism can have that covered though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-17T00:35:31-07:00","id":1130167,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1130157-lesser-ministries-anyone?p=1130164#post1130164\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Maybe this falls under Mammon, but I feel like there should be a Ministry whose philosophy is built around the Huxlian model of tyranny - keeping the populace in a docile content haze. Mammon consumerism can have that covered though.</div> </div> </div> </div>I am fairly sure that is what Pantechnicon, the other Chancellor ministry, is going for. Specifically through the use of comfortable and mysterious gadgetry. Keep Sleepers so occupied with their new toys that they do not waste thought on higher things.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Politeness is the lubricant of social intercourse.","edited":{"userid":272,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/272-saibot","user":"saibot","date":".  Correction 08-17-2017, 07:23 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/272-saibot","name":"saibot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar272_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1063"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-17T03:23:16-07:00","id":1130196,"title":"","content":"The emphasis on materialism that such a philosophy would entail does sound like a form of tyranny the Chancelor would spread. It's the Brave New World approach to oppressing the masses.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage","name":"Dusksage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3436_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-17T07:46:34-07:00","id":1130257,"title":"","content":"while I've never wrote it, I've always imagined that a Ministry dedicated to the Ruin would be something like this-<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I've always imagined the Ruin as a mad dancer who draws the whole world toward eternal doom as she spiral around himself, taking a place almost satanic to the other Iron Seal- not like the Gate, but near enough the bottom that the Seers know that worshiping her as a patron is not the smartest thing to do. I've always imagined her Ministry as an fatalistic cult, driven by pure nihilism. You are bound to a fate not your own, living a story written by another. They enforce the Lie by making others fall into such hopelessness, making them believe that they can't change the paths which was laid to them. They were to a certain class and die as such. Where the Prophet would focus on the great people who make history move, the Ruin would focus on the grey people who work like cogs in the machine- secretaries and bureaucrats, protesters and anarchists, spies and assassins. They are the faceless mob who brings the revolution and manage the terror afterwards. They are never in the front, never taking the place of the protagonists- but the mechanism which brings fourth the Deus Ex Machina.<br /> <br /> You never see the Ruin's climax to the plot before it's too late, but you always know that it is coming. That's the thing about good tragedies- you know how things would end, but you don't know how. You think the heroes are going to stop it, but each of their efforts just drives the story forward, toward their ultimate doom.<br /> <br /> Let the heroes take the front stage- they are the ones to die in the end. And when the applause would rise and everyone would cheer for the poisoned lovers or the stabbed knight, from behind the screen you would know that you fulfilled your role, and brought fourth the script just as your patron wrote it.<br /> <br /> yes, it was a fine tragedy. </div> </div> </div>and I've detailed my view of the Prophet's Ministry in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/560216-need-idea-for-a-lesser-ministry-dedicated-to-the-prophet\">here</a><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-17T09:51:16-07:00","id":1130321,"title":"","content":"Aren't Ministries global organizations, one for each Exarch? Even Lesser Ministries should commands dozens of pylons all over the world and have global influence.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11880-dark-archon","name":"Dark Archon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11880_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"348"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-17T11:27:25-07:00","id":1130367,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dark Archon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1130157-lesser-ministries-anyone?p=1130321#post1130321\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Aren't Ministries global organizations, one for each Exarch? Even Lesser Ministries should commands dozens of pylons all over the world and have global influence.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's actually a common misconception. Only the Great Ministries, and those who would contend with them, are truly global. Lesser Ministries are more akin to Nameless Orders in size and scope. The cost of not being a global power is offset by having these Ministries be far more specialized in purpose.<br /> <br /> For instance, the Seers of the Throne book gives the example of a Lesser Ministry that's operations and power base stretched as far as just one city. That Ministry was a potent power player in that city, but nowhere else. Because of that though even the Great Ministries would utilize that Lesser Ministry whenever they needed an operation done within that city. This made the Lesser Ministry valuable, but at the trade off of only being able to exert power within that city.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage","name":"Dusksage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3436_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-21T09:07:46-07:00","id":1132235,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1130157-lesser-ministries-anyone?p=1130164#post1130164\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Maybe this falls under Mammon, but I feel like there should be a Ministry whose philosophy is built around the Huxlian model of tyranny - keeping the populace in a docile content haze. Mammon consumerism can have that covered though.</div> </div> </div> </div>That sounds hell of a lot better than most Ministries. I'd expect it to be vastly more popular, especially if they sold themselves to newbies as a conspiracy dedicated to the advancement of quality of life through the alleviation of suffering in the world as we know it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3523-spencer-from-the-hills","name":"Spencer from The Hills","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"546"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-21T12:30:14-07:00","id":1132354,"title":"","content":"That's the Pantechnicon gig.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-21T15:15:09-07:00","id":1132408,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dusksage</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1130157-lesser-ministries-anyone#post1130157\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hi Wise Willworkers, Dusk here.<br /> <br /> Due to some friends of mine possibly getting into Mage the Awakening recently I delved back into some of my old PDFs, and as always had to re-read my favorite Mage Supplement: the Seers of the Throne Order book. I absolutely love those despicable bastards, and I might have gotten a bit carried away and made a few Lesser Ministries for possible future Mage Chronicles (technically I made two and updated one I made a while ago.) I feel compelled to share them with those who're interested in that sort of thing, and ask that if anyone else wants to share their own ideas or write ups for Lesser Ministries then if there isn't already a thread for that then there will be now. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> I short handed these to save word count, so they may be simplistic write ups. But I hope if nothing else they help illustrate why these shameless sellouts are so fascinating to me, and why they make such great foils for the Pentacle.<br /> <br /> <br /> \u2022 Homebrew Ministries <div align=\"center\">-snip-</div> ~ Charon<br /> &gt; Motto: &quot;As in life, so in death.&quot;<br /> &gt; Patron Exarch: The Psychopomp.<br /> &gt; Minister: The Director (It's not what it seems.)<br /> &gt; Tyranny: Manipulate people's worldly passions in life so that their anchors will be more easily controllable after death.<br /> &gt; Allies: Panopticon, Praetorian, and Mammon.<br /> &gt; Rivals: Paternoster, and all Lesser Ministries truly loyal to the Psychopomp. (More on that soon.)<br /> &gt; Plots: Charon's greatest asset is it's corporate Mystery Cult, Fulcrum International. In recent years the Ministry has invested countless resources into making it's pet corporation into a true power player in the world market. Today it can rival companies like the Deva Corporation and Last Dynasty International, and hungrily consumes lesser players into it's growing list of subsidiaries.<br /> &gt; Failings: The problem with Charon is that it's a Heretical Ministry. It's Minister, if it ever truly had one, has long been replaced by a powerful supernatural entity known only as the Director. While the Director still fulfills the same role as Minister, it's agenda is clearly more geared towards controlling ghosts and growing it's Mystery Cult. (The true nature of the Director is left purposefully vague so that it can better fit the needs of one's individual Chronicle. The only thing known for certain about it is that whether or not it's Supernal in nature it's well aware of the Wise and took over their organization so it could utilize their Supernal powers. One of my favorite personal theory about the Director is thus: It's the Supernal Symbol of Fulcrum International itself. The Ministry's use of the company as a sympathetic symbol led to it gaining Supernal weight and awareness. It see's itself as a nascent Exarch and seeks to use the Ministry to perform a &quot;hostile takeover&quot; and devour the Exarch of Death, thus replacing them.)<br /> &gt; Mysteries: Factories in the Underworld that mirror abandoned Fulcrum Facilities and staffed by the ghosts of former employees. Unique ghosts and other chthonic entities that defy the laws death. Bleeding-edge technology that serves as an anchor for ghosts, creating mechanical-ghost Claimed.<br /> &gt; Inspiration: Obviously Pentex and the Umbrella Corporation, but also Praxis from the podcast Alice Isn't Dead.</div> </div> </div> </div>Interesting but if I was using Seers of the Throne signature Arcanum as a critique of a particular aspect of modern and historic society as I often do, then I'd definitely go with &quot;death as the end&quot; instead of death as a transition (which is an observable objective Truth in the setting), remember the Lie is what keeps people oppressed, fear of death and oblivion to the point people can't even think or plan for their deaths/afterlives is the best possible outcome for the Exarchs. There is a strong trend in western culture to completely ignore this universal Truth of Death out of existential dread, almost everyone trying to stay young and pretend death isn't slowly stalking them in an inevitable predatory dance, and the thought of aging gracefully and facing death with hope and dignity is alien to a lot of people. It might seem paradoxical that a Ministry of Death would promote wild abandon and youth seeking but that's the role I see such a group could most effectively leverage the living and the dead. More people in denial of death's inexorability are more people unprepared to die, meaning more ghosts and those ghosts are more likely to be in denial as they were in life, making them easy pickings. Disbelief in the afterlife makes the living scoff at the idea of ghosts, so fewer are prepared and defended by superstitions or faith.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><i>\u201cYouth ages, immaturity is outgrown, ignorance can be educated, and drunkenness sobered, but stupid lasts forever.\u201d </i>~ <b>Aristophanes</b><br /> <i>&quot;Virescit Vulnere Virtus&quot;</i> ~ <b>Stewart Clan Motto</b></div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Frailty Chronicles</a></span><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">;</a><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Understanding the power of limitations.</a></b></div>","edited":{"userid":3279,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","user":"Pale_Crusader","date":". 08-21-2017, 06:19 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","name":"Pale_Crusader","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-22T01:05:20-07:00","id":1132524,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Pale_Crusader</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1130157-lesser-ministries-anyone?p=1132408#post1132408\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Interesting but if I was using Seers of the Throne signature Arcanum as a critique of a particular aspect of modern and historic society as I often do, then I'd definitely go with &quot;death as the end&quot; instead of death as a transition (which is an observable objective Truth in the setting), remember the Lie is what keeps people oppressed, fear of death and oblivion to the point people can't even think or plan for their deaths/afterlives is the best possible outcome for the Exarchs. There is a strong trend in western culture to completely ignore this universal Truth of Death out of existential dread, almost everyone trying to stay young and pretend death isn't slowly stalking them in an inevitable predatory dance, and the thought of aging gracefully and facing death with hope and dignity is alien to a lot of people. It might seem paradoxical that a Ministry of Death would promote wild abandon and youth seeking but that's the role I see such a group could most effectively leverage the living and the dead. More people in denial of death's inexorability are more people unprepared to die, meaning more ghosts and those ghosts are more likely to be in denial as they were in life, making them easy pickings. Disbelief in the afterlife makes the living scoff at the idea of ghosts, so fewer are prepared and defended by superstitions or faith.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not a bad idea indeed. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> The beauty of the Lesser Ministries is that they're just small enough that multiple takes on the Exarch's tyranny can both exist within the chronicle setting as different Lesser Ministries. And who knows, perhaps this Ministry of the Psychopomp won't get taken over by a sentient ghost-devouring super corporation...or by one of the Deceived and their cult from Mummy the Curse...or by the Contagion Chronicle version of itself...or whatever the hell you want the Director to actually be. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3436,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage","user":"Dusksage","date":".  Polish 08-22-2017, 04:07 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage","name":"Dusksage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3436_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-22T15:02:28-07:00","id":1132812,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dusksage</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1130157-lesser-ministries-anyone#post1130157\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">]\u2022 Homebrew Ministries<br /> <br /> ~ Hyades<br /> &gt; Motto: &quot;Abandon hope.&quot;<br /> &gt; Patron Exarch: The Ruin.<br /> &gt; Minister: Lorrian II, King of the Shrouded City.<br /> &gt; Tyranny: Cultivate defeatism and escapism through despair, tedium, and self-destructive habits.<br /> &gt; Allies: All four Great Ministries.<br /> &gt; Rivals: All other Lesser Ministries.<br /> &gt; Plots: The Ministry currently has Pylons working on weaponizing both corporate America and drug culture to further the Exarch's goals, but has yet to make inroads into the entertainment industry. Hyades seeks to remedy that as soon as possible since recent auguries indicate that doing so would allow further expansion for the Ministry.<br /> &gt; Failings: The Ministry is small compared to even some of the other Lesser Ministries. Hyades' reach only really extends to the Pacific North West of North America, and even then there are some regional Nameless Orders that are still larger in scope and influence. The fact that they remain active to this day is solely because they made themselves invaluable to the region's Tetrarchy.<br /> &gt; Mysteries: Artwork depicting abstract prophesies made by depressed Sleeper artists. A living office complex that feeds off the literal hopes and dreams of it's workers. A narcotic drug that traps non-lucid dreamers in an Astral Realm of languor while their bodies become comatose and highly susceptible to magical manipulation.<br /> &gt; Inspiration: Contemporary depictions of the King in Yellow's servants, and some depictions of the Lotus Eaters from the Odyssey.</div> </div> </div> </div>I really like this, the write up is wonderful and fits the Pacific Northwest well. However...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ruin</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"http://whitewolf.wikia.com/wiki/Ruin\" target=\"_blank\">Mystic destinies create new opportunities, but the Ruin ensures that people are skeptical and cynical about the opportunities ahead of them, thus binding them within the static cage of the Fallen World instead of pursuing their mystical destiny.</a></div> </div> </div> </div>Would seem better to fit an economic powers driving the Recession better than the Prosac Nation imagery I get from the wonderful write up you have. Given the drug themes and slavery to giving into instinctual carnal desires for comfort and promotion of ingesting pharmaceuticals there could be a better Patron:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Raptor</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"http://whitewolf.wikia.com/wiki/Raptor\" target=\"_blank\">He promotes faith in natural law, unleavened by free will. The world is predator and prey, rot and renewal, and individuals are helpless to choose how they flow along the world\u2019s life cycle. Instinct and resignation replace free will.</a></div> </div> </div> </div>I'd also inverse the inroads into entertainment, and make them more successful given how many great Ministries support them. Given the hypothetical changes there I'd leave the Narcotic Mystery but change the others to be more focused on the themes of destructive or apathetic indulgence of appetites. Examples: Shows that when binge watched in a particular order cause increasing levels of Soul loss, Prescription drugs that can make Sleepwalkers subject to Quiescence and even make Mages a source of Dissonance.<br /> <br /> <br /> I'd have a Ruin based Lesser Ministry be like this:<br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-size:18px\">Fiasconians</span></b><br /> <b>Motto: </b>&quot;Failing is our greatest success.&quot;<br /> <b>Minister:</b> Nostradamus<br /> <b>Tyranny: </b>Cultivate skepticism by promoting false prophecies.<br /> <b>Allies: </b>Panopticon, and Paternoster<br /> <b>Rivals: </b>Praetorians, Mammon, and Hegemony<br /> <b>Plots:</b> The Ministry currently has Pylons working on weaponizing both corporate News stations and crackpot internet sites to further the Exarch's goals. They are doing quite well with their allies in the Panopticon with these goals. It seems like every year is to be the last year of the world as we know it and this has made the public extremely jaded and deeply weary of the constant &quot;prophecies&quot;. It's gotten to the point no one takes them seriously at all and that's perfect because it damages people faith in destiny.<br /> <b>Failings: </b>Where this lesser ministry has done amazing things for the collective opinion about destiny individuals still persist to think they are somehow special and some even use the dire predictions to fantasize about something greater than their current lot. Fortunately only a very few slip through the cracks of fantasizing to actually doing anything in real life.<i> Also their campaign to create skeptics occasionally <a href=\"https://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.php/Main/GoneHorriblyRight\" target=\"_blank\">works just a little too well</a> for some individuals and they accidentally create peculiar Sleepwalkers called Fate Eaters whom are immune to the Fate Arcana and other Fate based powers, which interferes with changing mystical destinies to banal ones or even sensing their destiny (particularly problematic for Fate Eaters with innate mystical destiny which will comes to pass despite their disbelief). These Fate Eaters also mess up or destroy the strands of destiny of those they come into contact with, which often throws wrenches into the Fiasconian allies' machinations. The problems caused by Fate Eaters galvanizes the Pentacle against their Ministry specifically. Also because Fate Eaters can mess up Seer machinations which can't be pin pointed by Fate magic often leads to their allies using the Ministry as a convenient scape goat.</i><br /> <b>Mysteries:</b> Artwork depicting abstract prophesies made by depressed Sleeper artists. A chain e-mail that curses those that don't forward it. A living webpage making true predictions about the Stock Market but causes those to read it to disbelieve until it's too late.<br /> <b>Inspiration:</b> Mayan Calendar, y2k, Peek Oil, the News, Continental Solar Eclipses","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><i>\u201cYouth ages, immaturity is outgrown, ignorance can be educated, and drunkenness sobered, but stupid lasts forever.\u201d </i>~ <b>Aristophanes</b><br /> <i>&quot;Virescit Vulnere Virtus&quot;</i> ~ <b>Stewart Clan Motto</b></div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Frailty Chronicles</a></span><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">;</a><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Understanding the power of limitations.</a></b></div>","edited":{"userid":3279,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","user":"Pale_Crusader","date":".  Included Failings from http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1130157-lesser-ministries-anyone?p=1132821#post1132821 02-01-2022, 03:48 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","name":"Pale_Crusader","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-22T15:27:17-07:00","id":1132821,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Pale_Crusader</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1130157-lesser-ministries-anyone?p=1132812#post1132812\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'd have a Ruin based Lesser Ministry be like this:<br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-size:18px\">Fiasconians</span></b><br /> <b>Motto: </b>&amp;quot;Failing is our greatest success.&amp;quot;<br /> <b>Minister:</b> Nostradamus<br /> <b>Tyranny: </b>Cultivate skepticism by promoting false prophecies.<br /> <b>Allies: </b>Panopticon, and Paternoster<br /> <b>Rivals: </b>Praetorians, Mammon, and Hegemony<br /> <b>Plots:</b> The Ministry currently has Pylons working on weaponizing both corporate News stations and crackpot internet sites to further the Exarch's goals. They are doing quite well with their allies in the Panopticon with these goals. It seems like every year is to be the last year of the world as we know it and this has made the public extremely jaded and deeply weary of the constant &amp;quot;prophecies&amp;quot;. It's gotten to the point no one takes them seriously at all and that's perfect because it damages people faith in destiny.<br /> <b>Failings: </b>Where this lesser ministry has done amazing things for the collective opinion about destiny individuals still persist to think they are somehow special and some even use the dire predictions to fantasize about something greater than their current lot. Fortunately only a very few slip through the cracks of fantasizing to actually doing anything in real life.<br /> <b>Mysteries:</b> Artwork depicting abstract prophesies made by depressed Sleeper artists. A chain e-mail that curses those that don't forward it. A living webpage making true predictions about the Stock Market but causes those to read it to disbelieve until it's too late.<br /> <b>Inspiration:</b> Mayan Calendar, y2k, Peek Oil, the News, Continental Solar Eclipses</div> </div> </div> </div>Again, excellent work. I might have to borrow this idea for a future Chronicle sometime. My only critique about this is that their Failings isn't really a failings, more an acknowledgment of outliers. For Hyades and the rest of the examples I wanted to show the difficulties that naturally come from being a Lesser Ministry with the Failings (I.E. Specialized interests attract specialized opponents, small scale means heavy compromise, lesser scrutiny means higher chances for infiltration.)<br /> <br /> I feel a more interesting Failing would be something amongst the lines of: Their scepticism marketing campaign works just a little too well sometimes and they accidentally create unique Sleepwalkers called Fate Eaters who are immune to the Fate Arcana and other Fate based powers and who mess up or destroy the strands of destiny of those they come into contact with, which might be a good thing if it wasn't for the fact that this often ruins their allies mechanations and galvanizes the Pentacle against their Ministry specifically. This often leads to their allies using the Ministry as a convenient scape goat.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage","name":"Dusksage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3436_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-01T12:44:22-08:00","id":1473768,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dusksage</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1130157-lesser-ministries-anyone?p=1132821#post1132821\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I feel a more interesting Failing would be something amongst the lines of: Their scepticism marketing campaign works just a little too well sometimes and they accidentally create unique Sleepwalkers called Fate Eaters who are immune to the Fate Arcana and other Fate based powers and who mess up or destroy the strands of destiny of those they come into contact with, which might be a good thing if it wasn't for the fact that this often ruins their allies mechanations and galvanizes the Pentacle against their Ministry specifically. This often leads to their allies using the Ministry as a convenient scape goat.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Thank you. I liked your suggestion so much I edited my <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1130157-lesser-ministries-anyone?p=1132812#post1132812\">post</a> to include your idea as an addition. The addition is in italics.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><i>\u201cYouth ages, immaturity is outgrown, ignorance can be educated, and drunkenness sobered, but stupid lasts forever.\u201d </i>~ <b>Aristophanes</b><br /> <i>&quot;Virescit Vulnere Virtus&quot;</i> ~ <b>Stewart Clan Motto</b></div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Frailty Chronicles</a></span><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">;</a><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Understanding the power of limitations.</a></b></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","name":"Pale_Crusader","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"841"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}